we will store negative values so we know its was alreayd visited


Let's do a complete dry run, step by step, of the optimized solution for LeetCode 442: Find All Duplicates in an Array.

## Code we're dry-running

```
class Solution {
    public List<Integer> findDuplicates(int[] nums) {
        List<Integer> resList = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            int index = Math.abs(nums[i]) - 1; 
//Why subtract `1`? Because the numbers range from `1` to `n`, while array indices range from `0` to `n - 1`.
            if (nums[index] < 0) {
                resList.add(Math.abs(nums[i]));
            } else {
                nums[index] = -nums[index];
            }
        }

        return resList;
    }
}
```

