## 4. The key idea to remember

The most important line is:

```
int index = Math.abs(nums[i]) - 1;
```

Why subtract `1`? Because the numbers range from `1` to `n`, while array indices range from `0` to `n - 1`.

And this condition identifies duplicates:

```
if (nums[index] < 0)
```

- Positive: this number hasn't been marked yet.
- Negative: this number has already been encountered, so you've found a duplicate.

This gives you \\(O(n)\\) time and \\(O(1)\\) auxiliary space, excluding the output list.
